<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aundh Experiment</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a>–<a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aundh Experiment was a trial of village self-government in the princely state of Aundh, in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, launched in 1938 by its ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhawanrao-pant-pratinidhi">Bhawanrao Pant Pratinidhi</a>. On the advice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a>, the raja handed most powers to elected village <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panchayat">panchayats</a> and a state assembly under a constitution drafted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-frydman">Maurice Frydman</a>. It lasted until Aundh's merger into India in 1948.</p></div>
